== Display Stages ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Stage
! Description
|-
| Asset Transfer
| PI DMA transfers graphics and texture data from the ROM cartridge into RDRAM.
|-
| Command Queuing
| The CPU appends rendering commands to the RSP command queue in RDRAM.
|-
| RSP Processing
| The RSP reads commands from the queue, applies fixups, and writes RDP commands to a separate buffer in RDRAM.
|-
| RDP Signaling
| The RSP advances the RDP's end pointer (DP_END), directing it to execute the buffered commands.
|-
| Pixel Processing
| The RDP reads commands from RDRAM and performs rasterization, texture mapping, blending, and fill operations.
|-
| Framebuffer Write
| The RDP writes the rendered pixel data into the RDRAM framebuffer.
|-
| Framebuffer Commit
| The CPU writes the framebuffer address to VI_ORIGIN, directing the VI to read from it at the next vblank.
|-
| Scanout
| The VI reads the framebuffer and generates a digital video signal. Scaling, filtering, and color processing are applied according to VI register configuration.
|-
| Analog Output
| The Video DAC converts the digital video signal to analog output.
|}
